From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: link the display target to yaml-cpp

TerminalDisplay.h includes Config.h, which includes yaml-cpp headers. The
display target currently receives no yaml-cpp usage requirements: only the
final contour executable links that dependency. This breaks the display's
own compilation when yaml-cpp is fetched instead of installed globally.

Reuse the existing target selection for namespaced and legacy yaml-cpp
providers. Preserve the display target's existing plain linkage signature,
and guard the link for configurations without the GUI target.

Patch-Source: downstream adaptation of contour 0.6.3.8249 src/contour/CMakeLists.txt
Patch-License: Apache-2.0
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
Applies-To: contour 0.6.3.8249
Remove-When: upstream propagates yaml-cpp usage requirements to ContourTerminalDisplay
---
 src/contour/CMakeLists.txt | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/contour/CMakeLists.txt b/src/contour/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/contour/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/contour/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -175,3 +175,7 @@
 endif()
+if (TARGET ContourTerminalDisplay)
+    target_link_libraries(ContourTerminalDisplay ${YAML_CPP_LIBRARIES})
+endif()
+

 target_link_libraries(contour
